Upstream-Status: Accepted [https://github.com/OpenPrinting/libcupsfilters/commit/e14bad406189a66bdeb40131112944bfb58ee0cc]
Exit: Drop when freedesktop-sdk's libcupsfilters source includes e14bad406189a66bdeb40131112944bfb58ee0cc or an equivalent backport.
Subject: libcupsfilters: flush temporary PDF before counting pages

Backport OpenPrinting/libcupsfilters#167 to the SDK's 2.2.1 source.
cfPDFPagesFP() opens its temporary PDF through PDFio before flushing the
stdio writer. The missing tail can contain the cross-reference table and
trailer, causing "Missing Root object" and "Unexpected page count" errors
in both PDF-to-raster and PDF-to-PCL-XL printing.

Keep this in Dakota's patch queue, not the GNOME-synchronized SDK queue.
The upstream change is reduced to its functional fflush() addition.

Related: projectbluefin/dakota#1707

